# Command: SDD Restore

Command: /sdd-restore
Mode: SUPERVISED
Purpose: Restore .sdd/ files from backup

Description:
  Restores critical .sdd/ files from a previous backup.
  Requires human approval in SUPERVISED mode.
  Validates backup integrity before restore.

Usage:
  /sdd-restore --backup=<backup-name>
  /sdd-restore --latest
  /sdd-restore --list

Options:
  --backup=<name>   Restore from specific backup
  --latest          Restore from latest backup
  --list            List available backups
  --force           Skip confirmation (dangerous)

Restore Process:
  1. Load backup manifest
  2. Verify backup integrity (hashes)
  3. Create backup of current state (safety)
  4. Restore files from backup
  5. Verify restored files
  6. Update system state

Safety:
  - Current state backed up before restore
  - Backup integrity verified before restore
  - Human confirmation required (unless --force)
  - Restore logged in audit trail

Exit Codes:
  0 - Restore successful
  1 - Restore failed
  2 - Backup not found
  3 - Backup corrupted

State: +
